"description": "Prillfen Prill Tower PT-4 is a 12-head prill tower spraying 1.80 mm urea melt at 42 t/h when three heterogeneous, individually-correct agents jointly report 'melt-rate raise legal'. AIR's tower-mean air thermocouple is 82 C inside 75-90. SCRUB's scrubber NH3 mean is 18 ppm inside 8-30. SIZE's belt sampler is 1.80 mm inside 1.50-2.20. The conjunction is not a head-true certificate: shower-head SH-4 carries a 38 pct orifice shower-head plug. Uncommissioned SH-4 melt-film IR is 142 C against a 132 hold. Uncommissioned SH-4 plug camera is 38 pct against a 8.0 hold. AIR stays in-band because the tower-mean air model assumes open heads and never reads SH-4 IR. SCRUB stays in-band because SH-4's head is 1 of 6 and remains in auto. SIZE stays in-band because the belt sampler averages 12 heads and the plugged head is 1 of 12. Residual-first latches MELT-HOLD plus a melt-step probe; air-in-band-first would have authorized RAISE-MELT 42.0 to 51 t/h into a schedule-catchup window with SH-4 already plugged.",